1
00:00:10,814 --> 00:00:14,594
For such a tough guy, he
sure was easy to finish off.

2
00:00:15,614 --> 00:00:17,714
But I guess if you think about it,

3
00:00:18,134 --> 00:00:21,554
the end is usually a pretty
sudden curtain call, you know.

4
00:00:22,014 --> 00:00:24,031
Most folks don't get to say goodbye,

5
00:00:24,114 --> 00:00:26,871
especially when a bullet
to the brain's involved.

6
00:00:26,954 --> 00:00:27,784
Ha!

7
00:00:27,867 --> 00:00:31,518
Think of that as a little parting
wisdom before I make you croak.

8
00:00:34,034 --> 00:00:34,864
Polnareff!

9
00:00:34,947 --> 00:00:35,931
Don't let him get to you!

10
00:00:36,014 --> 00:00:37,838
You're much stronger than that!

11
00:00:38,034 --> 00:00:40,654
You still don't get it, do you? Mr.

12
00:00:40,794 --> 00:00:41,676
Avdol told you!

13
00:00:41,774 --> 00:00:43,715
He begged you not to fight alone!

14
00:00:44,874 --> 00:00:46,774
But you completely ignored him.

15
00:00:47,394 --> 00:00:51,331
Even if it meant dying with your enemy,
you were hell-bent on getting revenge.

16
00:00:51,414 --> 00:00:53,271
He followed you because that worried him.

17
00:00:53,354 --> 00:00:55,589
And this is what happened as a result!

18
00:00:55,934 --> 00:00:58,191
Then tell me, what am I supposed to do?

19
00:00:58,274 --> 00:01:00,234
We need to fall back for now.

20
00:01:02,374 --> 00:01:05,291
Avdol was stabbed in the back
and didn't have a chance.

21
00:01:05,374 --> 00:01:08,091
My sister couldn't defend
herself and was killed.

22
00:01:08,174 --> 00:01:11,591
You expect me to run away and
just forget all this happened?

23
00:01:11,674 --> 00:01:15,051
How can we fight them when we don't
even know what their stands can do?

24
00:01:15,134 --> 00:01:17,531
Don't fight a battle that'll
only end in your death!

25
00:01:17,614 --> 00:01:18,444
That's what Mr.

26
00:01:18,527 --> 00:01:20,160
Avdol was trying to tell you!

27
00:01:20,814 --> 00:01:22,214
Hey, come on.

28
00:01:22,354 --> 00:01:23,711
Do it, little pole pole.

29
00:01:23,794 --> 00:01:27,274
Why, you... Polnareff!

30
00:01:27,474 --> 00:01:29,591
Calm down and slowly retreat toward me.

31
00:01:29,674 --> 00:01:30,504
Got it?

32
00:01:30,587 --> 00:01:32,574
That truck's our way out of here. Calm?

33
00:01:32,854 --> 00:01:35,154
Calm down, you say? How?

34
00:01:45,414 --> 00:01:46,774
All right.

35
00:01:47,754 --> 00:01:48,584
Hey!

36
00:01:49,254 --> 00:01:50,084
Polnareff!

37
00:02:03,454 --> 00:02:06,774
It's your fault Avdol died, you know.

38
00:02:07,734 --> 00:02:10,234
I think that means you owe him.

39
00:02:10,394 --> 00:02:11,754
It only seems fair.

40
00:02:12,894 --> 00:02:16,134
Your friend bit the dust because of you.

41
00:02:16,894 --> 00:02:18,694
Damn you, you bastard.

42
00:02:19,094 --> 00:02:20,754
Where's your real body?

43
00:02:20,994 --> 00:02:22,494
Polnareff, calm down.

44
00:02:23,514 --> 00:02:26,374
But there's no need to be sad.

45
00:02:26,914 --> 00:02:29,034
Actually, you should be happy.

46
00:02:29,394 --> 00:02:32,374
You're about to see
your dear friend again.

47
00:02:32,914 --> 00:02:37,574
You'll soon be dead, and then you can
enjoy the afterlife with those two fools.

48
00:02:37,994 --> 00:02:38,914
You're welcome.

49
00:02:39,834 --> 00:02:44,594
I have to say, your
sister was so very sweet.

50
00:02:47,794 --> 00:02:54,294
Once you're reunited with your sister, Be
sure to ask her exactly how I killed her.

51
00:02:54,514 --> 00:02:56,134
We had such a ball.

52
00:02:57,874 --> 00:02:59,971
Klonorath, don't fall for his tricks.

53
00:03:00,054 --> 00:03:01,407
He wants you to attack.

54
00:03:02,054 --> 00:03:02,884
Master!

55
00:03:08,954 --> 00:03:10,334
Oh, didn't you know?

56
00:03:10,554 --> 00:03:13,354
Your chariot cannot cut my hanged man.

57
00:03:16,314 --> 00:03:22,834
I'm in the mirror where your
stand can't go that's why.

58
00:03:25,474 --> 00:03:29,071
So close and yet so far away.

59
00:03:29,154 --> 00:03:36,074
Whole horse fire away let's put
an end to this idiot aye aye sir!

60
00:03:41,374 --> 00:03:42,294
Die!

61
00:03:42,994 --> 00:03:45,214
Hammer roll! Flash!

62
00:03:51,254 --> 00:03:52,394
What the?

63
00:03:52,634 --> 00:03:54,614
Wait, he's shot! Hold around!

64
00:04:05,914 --> 00:04:06,971
Cuckooing, was it?

65
00:04:07,054 --> 00:04:08,254
Not bad, partner.

66
00:04:12,234 --> 00:04:13,911
That's out of my stance range.

67
00:04:13,994 --> 00:04:18,582
Even if I got him from here, the bullet
wouldn't hit him with very much force.

68
00:04:20,794 --> 00:04:22,374
He went after them, huh?

69
00:04:22,634 --> 00:04:23,594
Well, I'll be.

70
00:04:24,614 --> 00:04:26,974
He must really have it in for Polnareff.

71
00:04:31,014 --> 00:04:33,654
I'm so sorry, Kakuhin.

72
00:04:35,394 --> 00:04:36,811
It's just that...

73
00:04:36,894 --> 00:04:42,234
I thought so long as I could avenge my
sister, I wouldn't care if I lived or died.

74
00:04:42,794 --> 00:04:44,594
But I understand now.

75
00:04:45,194 --> 00:04:47,514
I know Avdol was fighting for me.

76
00:04:48,154 --> 00:04:50,554
His sacrifice won't be for naught.

77
00:04:51,474 --> 00:04:53,374
I'll fight to keep on living.

78
00:04:54,654 --> 00:04:57,360
You sure that you really
mean that, Polnareff?

79
00:04:57,894 --> 00:04:58,724
Oui.

80
00:05:01,094 --> 00:05:04,918
That's all I'm giving you is proof
that we've made up, Polnareff.

81
00:05:06,194 --> 00:05:07,024
Right.

82
00:05:07,107 --> 00:05:08,314
Merci, Kakyoin.

83
00:05:09,174 --> 00:05:13,645
When those bastards come after us again,
I swear we'll defeat them together.

84
00:05:20,374 --> 00:05:22,374
Avdol, my old friend.

85
00:05:32,334 --> 00:05:33,164
You know,

86
00:05:33,434 --> 00:05:39,054
I was so sure that I stabbed him with
my sword, but my strike never hit him.

87
00:05:39,454 --> 00:05:41,274
It was like he wasn't there.

88
00:05:45,154 --> 00:05:47,931
Even breaking the mirror
into pieces didn't stop him.

89
00:05:48,014 --> 00:05:49,911
The hanged man just
attacked from the shards.

90
00:05:49,994 --> 00:05:52,791
How in the hell am I supposed
to fight against that?

91
00:05:52,874 --> 00:05:54,514
He attacks your reflection.

92
00:05:54,614 --> 00:06:00,051
But his knife sinks into your real flesh
and my stand can't go inside mirrors

93
00:06:00,134 --> 00:06:05,154
How are we supposed to attack him if he's
in some kind of mirror world damn it?

94
00:06:06,894 --> 00:06:10,671
Polnareff you keep talking about
inside the mirror in the mirror

95
00:06:10,754 --> 00:06:14,891
world But there's no such thing
as a world in a mirror remember.

96
00:06:14,974 --> 00:06:17,014
This is reality not fantasy

97
00:06:17,974 --> 00:06:20,474
What are you talking about you saw it too?

98
00:06:20,694 --> 00:06:25,251
Didn't you you can only see him in a mirror
and when you turn around he's gone Yes.

99
00:06:25,334 --> 00:06:29,191
But anything that you see in a mirror
is just a reflection created by light.

100
00:06:29,274 --> 00:06:30,614
I'm not an idiot!

101
00:06:30,834 --> 00:06:32,271
You don't have to tell me that!

102
00:06:32,354 --> 00:06:34,134
Listen, I mean this case.

103
00:06:34,314 --> 00:06:36,191
I'm talking about what's going on now.

104
00:06:36,274 --> 00:06:39,911
If Stans can exist in this world,
there could be a mirror world too.

105
00:06:39,994 --> 00:06:40,824
There isn't.

106
00:06:40,994 --> 00:06:42,254
Come on, man!

107
00:06:43,234 --> 00:06:48,194
I think that fact is what's going to help
us solve the mystery of Hanged Man. Look,

108
00:06:48,434 --> 00:06:50,591
Stans are able to destroy other Stans,

109
00:06:50,674 --> 00:06:53,451
so there still has to be something
we don't know about his...

110
00:06:53,534 --> 00:06:54,364
Hmm?

111
00:07:07,414 --> 00:07:08,244
Polnareff!

112
00:07:08,327 --> 00:07:09,791
The chrome of the steering wheel!

113
00:07:09,874 --> 00:07:10,704
What?

114
00:07:10,787 --> 00:07:12,040
The bastards caught up to us!

115
00:07:12,474 --> 00:07:13,374
Look out!

116
00:07:27,194 --> 00:07:28,614
Hey, are you okay?

117
00:07:28,894 --> 00:07:30,411
Talk to me. I...

118
00:07:30,494 --> 00:07:33,074
I slammed my chest, but I'll be fine.

119
00:07:35,894 --> 00:07:36,724
What?

120
00:07:41,514 --> 00:07:42,344
Charion!

121
00:07:44,654 --> 00:07:46,574
Kick, avoid the reflection!

122
00:07:54,314 --> 00:07:55,514
Damn. I got it.

123
00:07:55,714 --> 00:07:56,954
I just saw him do it.

124
00:07:57,734 --> 00:07:59,675
He's going from mirror to mirror.

125
00:07:59,914 --> 00:08:03,443
This guy moves by jumping around,
one reflection to another.

126
00:08:04,734 --> 00:08:08,194
He traveled all this way by
reflecting over and over.

127
00:08:08,434 --> 00:08:11,554
It's the only explanation
for how he caught up to us.

128
00:08:12,954 --> 00:08:13,784
Reflecting?

129
00:08:13,867 --> 00:08:15,298
That means he's actually light.

130
00:08:15,474 --> 00:08:18,211
Are you saying that the true
nature of his stand is light?

131
00:08:18,294 --> 00:08:19,124
I am.

132
00:08:19,254 --> 00:08:21,313
I just saw him in the car's bumper.

133
00:08:21,594 --> 00:08:24,751
He's going to reflect off that
surface and onto something else.

134
00:08:24,834 --> 00:08:26,658
Stay clear of reflective stuff.

135
00:08:26,894 --> 00:08:30,131
Take anything shiny off your
body and your uniform button.

136
00:08:30,214 --> 00:08:32,038
Hey, mister, are you guys okay?

137
00:08:32,654 --> 00:08:34,431
Want me to bring you some medicine?

138
00:08:34,514 --> 00:08:35,344
We're fine.

139
00:08:35,427 --> 00:08:36,257
Look, it's dangerous.

140
00:08:36,340 --> 00:08:37,235
Get out of here.

141
00:08:37,454 --> 00:08:40,334
Whoa, you guys totally messed up your car.

142
00:08:41,294 --> 00:08:43,434
Hey, you're bleeding, mister.

143
00:08:44,594 --> 00:08:46,434
Are you sure you're okay?

144
00:08:50,634 --> 00:08:51,594
That asshole!

145
00:08:51,854 --> 00:08:53,736
He's reflected in the kid's eye!

146
00:08:55,814 --> 00:08:58,194
Listen, kid, don't look at us! Huh?

147
00:08:58,474 --> 00:09:00,854
I told you, don't look at us!

148
00:09:02,374 --> 00:09:04,091
Don't follow me with your eyes!

149
00:09:04,174 --> 00:09:05,004
Huh?

150
00:09:05,087 --> 00:09:05,917
But your heart!

151
00:09:06,294 --> 00:09:07,131
I'm fine, see?

152
00:09:07,214 --> 00:09:08,551
Perfectly fine, got it?

153
00:09:08,634 --> 00:09:10,871
So go look over there! But...

154
00:09:10,954 --> 00:09:12,130
but you're bleeding!

155
00:09:12,234 --> 00:09:13,831
You brat, I said look over there!

156
00:09:13,914 --> 00:09:14,744
Huh?

157
00:09:16,854 --> 00:09:18,894
Damn you, Xeniphaled!

158
00:09:19,214 --> 00:09:20,685
What are you going to do?

159
00:09:20,774 --> 00:09:24,231
You wouldn't poke out this cute little
kid's eye with that sword of yours,

160
00:09:24,314 --> 00:09:25,144
would you?

161
00:09:25,794 --> 00:09:26,624
Polnareff!

162
00:09:27,974 --> 00:09:28,804
Polnareff!

163
00:09:28,887 --> 00:09:30,794
And now I finally got you!

164
00:09:31,054 --> 00:09:32,534
You can't run anymore.

165
00:09:32,834 --> 00:09:35,254
Not unless you gouge the kid's eyes out.

166
00:09:37,474 --> 00:09:40,474
You disgusting, cruel son
of a bitch! You're dead!

167
00:09:48,454 --> 00:09:49,934
Don't worry, Kakyoini.

168
00:09:50,614 --> 00:09:53,849
Mon frere, that's not what
you say at a time like this.

169
00:09:54,154 --> 00:09:58,054
Listen, in times like these, you've
got to say something fitting.

170
00:09:58,394 --> 00:10:01,806
Before you get your revenge,
say something like this here.

171
00:10:03,174 --> 00:10:05,814
My name is Jean-Pierre Polnareff.

172
00:10:05,934 --> 00:10:08,271
For the honor of my dearest sister's soul,

173
00:10:08,354 --> 00:10:11,691
and so my good friend Avdol can
rest peacefully in heaven above?

174
00:10:11,774 --> 00:10:14,656
I'm going to hurl you into
the depths of despair!

175
00:10:15,574 --> 00:10:17,674
Prepare yourself, centerfold!

176
00:10:18,874 --> 00:10:20,294
Sorry about this, kid.

177
00:10:20,534 --> 00:10:23,063
I'll buy you whatever
candy you want, okay?

178
00:10:23,634 --> 00:10:25,634
You got dead in my eyes!

179
00:10:34,934 --> 00:10:35,764
What the?

180
00:10:35,847 --> 00:10:37,031
Polnareff, he's in your eye!

181
00:10:37,114 --> 00:10:41,111
I don't really understand how, but he
essentially moves at the speed of light.

182
00:10:41,194 --> 00:10:43,774
No one can normally see speed like that.

183
00:10:43,974 --> 00:10:48,111
But then, I knew that if the kid closed
his eyes, the next move would be to my eye.

184
00:10:48,194 --> 00:10:51,411
There was no other place for him to
go, and that's how we'll beat him.

185
00:10:51,494 --> 00:10:52,354
Oh, I see.

186
00:10:52,874 --> 00:10:56,227
Hanged man can only exist
within the world of reflection.

187
00:10:58,554 --> 00:11:01,014
When one world is about to be destroyed,

188
00:11:01,374 --> 00:11:04,021
he must migrate to
another reflective object.

189
00:11:05,014 --> 00:11:10,194
So, as long as I can read his trajectory,
I can slice through him like butter!

190
00:11:11,194 --> 00:11:13,554
His real body is over there.

191
00:11:15,414 --> 00:11:18,134
You bastard. Finally.

192
00:11:19,814 --> 00:11:20,974
Finally!

193
00:11:30,674 --> 00:11:33,214
At last we meet.

194
00:11:35,514 --> 00:11:36,674
Centerfold!

195
00:11:39,734 --> 00:11:42,431
My name is Jean-Pierre Polnareff,

196
00:11:42,514 --> 00:11:45,371
and I've seen through your
stand's clever little trick.

197
00:11:45,454 --> 00:11:48,774
It's a stand of light that
moves at extraordinary speed.

198
00:11:49,134 --> 00:11:51,411
I know there's no way that I can catch it,

199
00:11:51,494 --> 00:11:54,911
but if I can predict where your
stand's going to jump next,

200
00:11:54,994 --> 00:11:59,094
and I slash its trajectory in
that moment, I can cut you.

201
00:11:59,974 --> 00:12:02,494
If Kakyoin and Avdol hadn't shown up,

202
00:12:02,614 --> 00:12:06,790
I probably wouldn't have figured that
out and you would have killed me.

203
00:12:07,194 --> 00:12:08,374
No, Polnareff!

204
00:12:08,534 --> 00:12:10,811
This isn't the man with
a pair of right hands!

205
00:12:10,894 --> 00:12:12,188
That's not Cinderbolt!

206
00:12:17,634 --> 00:12:19,314
What the hell?

207
00:12:20,854 --> 00:12:21,684
Polnareff!

208
00:12:31,474 --> 00:12:32,304
Polnareff!

209
00:12:35,594 --> 00:12:36,674
Over here!

210
00:12:41,914 --> 00:12:44,934
I'm centerfold, insignificant fool!

211
00:12:45,314 --> 00:12:46,434
At last!

212
00:12:46,814 --> 00:12:50,873
That man is some beggar who was in
the wrong place at the wrong time.

213
00:12:51,094 --> 00:12:56,274
I just carved a small wound in him, the
same wound you were so gracious to give me.

214
00:12:57,914 --> 00:13:00,291
You totally fell for it.

215
00:13:00,374 --> 00:13:04,471
Getting close to him without knowing
what I look like was a grave mistake.

216
00:13:04,554 --> 00:13:07,434
One you'll pay for with your limes!

217
00:13:08,794 --> 00:13:09,994
You bastard!

218
00:13:11,294 --> 00:13:13,194
Take this! Emerald!

219
00:13:13,874 --> 00:13:14,704
Whoa!

220
00:13:14,787 --> 00:13:15,617
Wait now!

221
00:13:15,700 --> 00:13:16,681
Take a good look around you!

222
00:13:19,094 --> 00:13:19,924
Hey!

223
00:13:20,007 --> 00:13:20,837
Gather round!

224
00:13:21,634 --> 00:13:23,114
See these two gentlemen?

225
00:13:23,434 --> 00:13:26,316
They say they've got a
boatload of cash to share!

226
00:13:28,674 --> 00:13:31,371
what you'll give us money for nothing huh?

227
00:13:31,454 --> 00:13:33,471
such generosity you have?

228
00:13:33,554 --> 00:13:35,434
such big heart? thank you!

229
00:13:39,834 --> 00:13:42,814
have you figured out what's going on yet?

230
00:13:45,394 --> 00:13:47,851
you say you figured out my stand?

231
00:13:47,934 --> 00:13:49,051
you fool?

232
00:13:49,134 --> 00:13:51,534
you think i don't know my own weakness?

233
00:13:54,834 --> 00:13:56,291
i have no weakness?

234
00:13:56,374 --> 00:13:58,551
you can never know
where i'll jump to next?

235
00:13:58,634 --> 00:14:00,851
don't look?

236
00:14:00,934 --> 00:14:02,291
don't stare at us!

237
00:14:02,374 --> 00:14:03,291
please?

238
00:14:03,374 --> 00:14:04,631
just look away!

239
00:14:04,714 --> 00:14:07,551
you can't run anymore!

240
00:14:07,634 --> 00:14:09,611
what are you going to do?

241
00:14:09,694 --> 00:14:10,934
blow everyone up!

242
00:14:13,274 --> 00:14:15,491
you sacrificed your entire youth?

243
00:14:15,574 --> 00:14:16,571
just taught me down?

244
00:14:16,654 --> 00:14:18,231
and just when you're close?

245
00:14:18,314 --> 00:14:19,144
you're going?

246
00:14:19,227 --> 00:14:20,614
to fail to avenge your sister?

247
00:14:20,874 --> 00:14:22,914
How pathetic and sad. Meanwhile,

248
00:14:23,274 --> 00:14:28,071
I, Centrifold, will continue a life surrounded
by young beauties, like your sister.

249
00:14:28,154 --> 00:14:29,214
I can see it now.

250
00:14:29,494 --> 00:14:30,614
Oh, the pleasures.

251
00:14:32,654 --> 00:14:35,419
Come to think of it, that
sweet sister of yours

252
00:14:36,054 --> 00:14:38,094
was really good at sobbing.

253
00:14:43,794 --> 00:14:44,624
Farewell.

254
00:14:45,734 --> 00:14:46,564
Why, you?

255
00:14:47,074 --> 00:14:47,904
Polnarex.

256
00:14:47,987 --> 00:14:49,894
You could do better than that. Huh?

257
00:14:50,394 --> 00:14:51,982
Why you isn't what you say?

258
00:14:52,134 --> 00:14:55,016
When taking revenge, you
have to be more refined.

259
00:14:55,174 --> 00:14:56,494
This is what you say.

260
00:14:57,854 --> 00:15:00,014
My name is Noriaki Kakyoin.

261
00:15:00,394 --> 00:15:02,894
In order to avenge my dear friend Avdol,

262
00:15:03,214 --> 00:15:08,096
so that the soul of my friend Polnarev's
sister may rest in peace for all eternity?

263
00:15:10,414 --> 00:15:12,614
I will have you pay with your life.

264
00:15:14,234 --> 00:15:17,574
I'll give this gold coin to
whoever picks it up. Behold!

265
00:15:17,874 --> 00:15:20,403
A coin so perfect, it
shines like a mirror!

266
00:15:20,674 --> 00:15:22,474
Yeah, now I see.

267
00:15:26,134 --> 00:15:30,194
Looks like all of their eyes are
focused on one point now. Yeah.

268
00:15:32,554 --> 00:15:35,907
We know the trajectory that
Hanged Man will have to take.

269
00:15:36,994 --> 00:15:38,454
Merci, Capuin!

270
00:15:50,414 --> 00:15:51,244
Now!

271
00:16:00,314 --> 00:16:01,194
Hold it!

272
00:16:06,234 --> 00:16:07,594
It won't open!

273
00:16:09,054 --> 00:16:13,114
Looks like you're the one who's
really good at sobbing, Centerfold.

274
00:16:14,014 --> 00:16:18,694
and you're about to plummet into hell,
begging and crying the whole way down.

275
00:16:19,294 --> 00:16:23,176
But there's one thing I can't rely
on the Guardians of Hell to do.

276
00:16:23,474 --> 00:16:28,534
And that's to turn your
body into a pincushion.

277
00:16:32,734 --> 00:16:35,294
I've been waiting years for this moment.

278
00:16:47,874 --> 00:16:50,814
I'll leave the rest to
the devil, rot in hell.

279
00:16:51,294 --> 00:16:53,834
So this is the true hanged man, huh?

280
00:16:54,154 --> 00:16:56,694
He was rotten all the way to the core.

281
00:17:00,974 --> 00:17:02,794
I got my revenge.

282
00:17:13,334 --> 00:17:14,254
Hold it!

283
00:17:17,574 --> 00:17:19,162
Finally caught up with you!

284
00:17:26,974 --> 00:17:29,074
Why are you walking so slow?

285
00:17:29,754 --> 00:17:33,094
If you're gonna run, run
like your lives depend on it.

286
00:17:33,234 --> 00:17:34,374
It's way more fun.

287
00:17:34,974 --> 00:17:37,114
Isn't that right, Mr. Cinefold?

288
00:17:40,634 --> 00:17:42,734
Better say your prayers, boys.

289
00:17:43,114 --> 00:17:45,211
This is where your lives come to an end.

290
00:17:45,294 --> 00:17:48,111
Come at us with everything
you've got, understand?

291
00:17:48,194 --> 00:17:52,654
It's so boring if you just stand
there and die. Right, Mr. Centerfold?

292
00:18:00,934 --> 00:18:01,894
Hey, Mr.

293
00:18:02,134 --> 00:18:04,051
Centerfold, aren't you going to play?

294
00:18:04,134 --> 00:18:07,294
I don't think he's listening
anymore, cowboy. Huh?

295
00:18:08,534 --> 00:18:10,694
He's quite busy at the moment.

296
00:18:11,374 --> 00:18:13,654
Carrying out his sentence in hell.

297
00:18:18,694 --> 00:18:20,576
Don't try to pull that nonsense.

298
00:18:20,974 --> 00:18:22,503
Bluffing won't work on me.

299
00:18:22,694 --> 00:18:23,694
Nice try, though.

300
00:18:24,934 --> 00:18:27,346
There's no way you could have beaten him.

301
00:18:27,994 --> 00:18:31,434
Even I wouldn't try my
luck against that mother.

302
00:18:32,474 --> 00:18:35,298
You know, Polnareff, your
sense of humor stinks.

303
00:18:36,454 --> 00:18:39,311
That piece of shit's corpse is 2 or 3,000

304
00:18:39,394 --> 00:18:41,451
meters that way if you
want to take a look.

305
00:18:41,534 --> 00:18:42,364
Huh?

306
00:18:43,374 --> 00:18:45,094
Okay, I will. Huh?

307
00:18:45,614 --> 00:18:46,894
You're running away?

308
00:18:47,954 --> 00:18:49,514
I don't stand a chance.

309
00:18:49,754 --> 00:18:51,691
I'm at a total disadvantage by myself.

310
00:18:51,774 --> 00:18:55,303
I'm hightailing it out of here,
waiting for a better chance.

311
00:18:55,654 --> 00:18:59,595
Or better yet, waiting till I find
myself another partner in crime.

312
00:19:00,474 --> 00:19:02,356
It's all about being number two.

313
00:19:02,674 --> 00:19:04,733
That's the motto I like to live by.

314
00:19:04,874 --> 00:19:06,334
Got a problem with it.

315
00:19:08,634 --> 00:19:09,464
What?

316
00:19:12,894 --> 00:19:13,724
Mr.

317
00:19:13,807 --> 00:19:14,954
Joestar, Jotaral!

318
00:19:16,714 --> 00:19:19,394
We already know about
Avdol. What a tragedy.

319
00:19:20,454 --> 00:19:25,278
We didn't have a lot of time to do much
for him, but we gave him a proper funeral.

320
00:19:29,494 --> 00:19:30,954
The one who stabbed Mr.

321
00:19:31,114 --> 00:19:33,891
Avdol in the back was the
man with two right hands.

322
00:19:33,974 --> 00:19:36,798
But the cause of death
was Whole Horse's bullet.

323
00:19:37,594 --> 00:19:39,182
What should we do with him?

324
00:19:39,414 --> 00:19:41,002
I'll give him his sentence!

325
00:19:48,334 --> 00:19:49,164
DEATH!

326
00:19:51,974 --> 00:19:53,614
Please run, Sir Hall Horse!

327
00:19:54,154 --> 00:19:55,625
I'll hold him up for you!

328
00:19:55,714 --> 00:19:56,544
The hell?

329
00:19:56,627 --> 00:19:57,457
Get off, lady!

330
00:19:57,540 --> 00:20:01,095
I don't know what exactly is going on here,
but I do know I will always protect you!

331
00:20:01,254 --> 00:20:04,914
You are my everything,
darling! Please run! Hurry!

332
00:20:05,874 --> 00:20:07,771
Let go of me, stupid bitch!

333
00:20:07,854 --> 00:20:09,074
Come on!

334
00:20:09,254 --> 00:20:11,994
What are you doing? Jotaro! Kakyoin!

335
00:20:12,174 --> 00:20:13,831
Don't let Hull Horse get away!

336
00:20:13,914 --> 00:20:15,274
It's too late.

337
00:20:18,314 --> 00:20:20,614
Very well said, my little sweetheart.

338
00:20:20,974 --> 00:20:24,054
I'll gladly accept your
feelings and keep on living.

339
00:20:25,214 --> 00:20:28,567
Remember, I'm only running
away because I love you, baby!

340
00:20:29,174 --> 00:20:30,494
Forever and ever!

341
00:20:32,314 --> 00:20:33,474
Why, you!

342
00:20:34,194 --> 00:20:35,674
Come back here!

343
00:20:39,954 --> 00:20:42,174
Oh, don't you dare aww at me!

344
00:20:44,434 --> 00:20:45,264
Polnareff!

345
00:20:45,347 --> 00:20:47,840
That woman is just another
one of his victims.

346
00:20:48,534 --> 00:20:51,774
And he no longer had any
intention of fighting with us.

347
00:20:51,914 --> 00:20:53,855
We have no time to deal with him.

348
00:20:56,694 --> 00:20:58,254
Evdal is gone now.

349
00:20:58,814 --> 00:21:00,554
But we have to forge ahead.

350
00:21:03,274 --> 00:21:05,254
It's already been fifteen days.

351
00:21:05,474 --> 00:21:07,121
We don't have time to waste.

352
00:21:11,294 --> 00:21:12,214
Damn it.

353
00:21:13,374 --> 00:21:14,894
Guess it can't be helped.

354
00:21:18,654 --> 00:21:21,414
Alright, we continue onward to Egypt.

355
00:21:21,934 --> 00:21:22,764
Listen up.

356
00:21:22,847 --> 00:21:25,814
In order to defeat Dio,
we have to fight as one.

357
00:21:26,114 --> 00:21:31,614
We can't go off on our own, or we'll play
right into the enemy's hands. Got it?

358
00:21:33,334 --> 00:21:34,854
Let's get a move on!

359
00:21:36,914 --> 00:21:37,874
Good grief.

360
00:22:12,254 --> 00:22:14,931
All the old paintings on the tomb.

361
00:22:15,014 --> 00:22:16,991
They do the sand dance, don't you know?

362
00:22:17,074 --> 00:22:18,614
If they move too quick.

363
00:22:19,294 --> 00:22:21,631
They're falling down like a domino.

364
00:22:21,714 --> 00:22:24,311
All the birds are men by the Nile.

365
00:22:24,394 --> 00:22:26,351
They've got their money on a bed.

366
00:22:26,434 --> 00:22:27,951
Called crocodiles.

367
00:22:28,034 --> 00:22:30,931
They snap their teeth on your cigarette.

368
00:22:31,014 --> 00:22:33,334
Falling tight to the hookah. I say.

369
00:22:39,934 --> 00:22:42,154
Walk like an Egyptian.

370
00:22:53,934 --> 00:22:55,531
The blonde waitresses.

371
00:22:55,614 --> 00:22:56,931
Take their trays.

372
00:22:57,014 --> 00:22:58,931
Spin around and they cross the floor.

373
00:22:59,014 --> 00:23:00,451
They've got the moves.

374
00:23:00,534 --> 00:23:02,371
You drop, you drink.

375
00:23:02,454 --> 00:23:03,591
Then they bring you more.

376
00:23:03,674 --> 00:23:06,231
All the school kids so sick of books.

377
00:23:06,314 --> 00:23:08,291
They're like the punk and the metal band.

378
00:23:08,374 --> 00:23:09,874
When the buzzer rings.

379
00:23:10,614 --> 00:23:12,531
They're walking like an Egyptian.

380
00:23:12,614 --> 00:23:15,631
All the kids in the marketplace say. Walk

381
00:23:15,714 --> 00:23:22,714
like

382
00:23:23,354 --> 00:23:24,184
an Egyptian.

383
00:23:27,194 --> 00:23:28,394
We're almost there.

384
00:23:28,514 --> 00:23:30,731
The city of Varanasi. Varanasi!

385
00:23:30,814 --> 00:23:31,791
I got him!

386
00:23:31,874 --> 00:23:34,874
I'm Joseph Joestar, an American! What?

387
00:23:35,294 --> 00:23:36,254
I love you.

388
00:23:36,374 --> 00:23:39,454
Hey, doesn't that sort of
look like a person's face?

389
00:23:39,974 --> 00:23:40,954
Show me me!
